From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:33:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] VPVulkan: VK_EXT_host_image_copy

vkCopyMemoryToImageEXT / vkCopyImageToMemoryEXT / vkCopyImageToImageEXT /
vkTransitionImageLayoutEXT / vkGetImageSubresourceLayout2(KHR|EXT). Images live in Metal private
storage (replaceRegion cannot reach them), so each call is a staged GPU copy submitted alone and
waited for (that frame only): host memory -> page-aligned staging buffer -> texture and back,
with memoryRowLength / memoryImageHeight pitches. Layout transitions are no-ops. Properties list
every layout; image format queries accept HOST_TRANSFER usage and answer the performance query;
VkFormatProperties3 reports HOST_IMAGE_TRANSFER. Completes Alyx's captured extension list
(gpu_vulkan.alyx creates the device with all of them).

Test: gpu_vulkan.host_image_copy.

